lesson: 91
title: Counting coins
stars: 0
explain: A penny is worth 1 cent, a nickel 5 cents, a dime 10 cents and a quarter 25 cents.
explain: To count coins, find the value of each kind and add them: 2 quarters, 3 dimes, 2 nickels and 4 pennies
explain: are 50 + 30 + 10 + 4 = 94 cents.
vars: a=name q=2..4 d=2..6 k=2..5 p=2..9
answer: q * 25 + d * 10 + k * 5 + p
exercise: {a} has {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents does {a.he} have?
exercise: In {a}'s pocket there are {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents is that in all?
exercise: {a} finds {p} pennies, {k} nickels, {d} dimes and {q} quarters in a jar. How much money is in the jar, in cents?
exercise: A purse holds {d} dimes, {q} quarters, {p} pennies and {k} nickels. What is the total value in cents?
exercise: {a} counts {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents does {a.he} count?
exercise: There are {k} nickels, {p} pennies, {q} quarters and {d} dimes on the table. How many cents are on the table?
test: {a} empties {a.his} piggy bank: out come {q} quarters, {k} nickels, {d} dimes and {p} pennies. What are the coins worth in cents?
test: How many cents do {p} pennies, {d} dimes, {q} quarters and {k} nickels make together?
test: {a} pays for a toy with {d} dimes, {k} nickels, {p} pennies and {q} quarters. How many cents does the toy cost?
test: {a} saved {q} quarters and {d} dimes in May, and {k} nickels and {p} pennies in June. How many cents did {a.he} save in the two months?
exercise: How many cents altogether are {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies?
exercise: {a} has {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies in total. What is the money worth in cents?
exercise: Coins in a jar: {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels, {p} pennies. How many cents?
exercise: {a} lives in Ohio and keeps {d} dimes, {p} pennies, {q} quarters and {k} nickels in a box. How many cents are in the box?
exercise: {a} puts {q.words} quarters, {d.words} dimes, {k.words} nickels and {p.words} pennies on the desk. How many cents is that?
exercise: {a} gets {k} nickels and {p} pennies from {a.his} aunt and {q} quarters and {d} dimes from {a.his} uncle. How many cents does {a.he} get combined?
exercise: What is the total value, in cents, of {p} pennies, {k} nickels, {q} quarters and {d} dimes?
exercise: A wallet holds {q} quarters, {k} nickels, {d} dimes and {p} pennies. How many cents are in the wallet?
test: {a} sorts the change in {a.his} coat pocket into piles: {p} pennies, {q} quarters, {k} nickels and {d} dimes. How many cents does {a.he} have in all?
test: At a yard sale in Maine, {a} takes {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies. How much money is that, in cents?
test: Find the value in cents of these coins together: {d} dimes, {q} quarters, {p} pennies, {k} nickels.
test: {a} trades {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies for a single bill. How many cents are the coins worth?
test: A vending machine in Florida holds {k} nickels, {d} dimes, {q} quarters and {p} pennies. How many cents are inside it?
test: {a}'s little brother drops {q.words} quarters, {d.words} dimes, {k.words} nickels and {p.words} pennies into a tin. How many cents are in the tin?
