test: {a} says it's {q+d+k+p} cents cos that's how many coins. nah — {q} quarters {d} dimes {k} nickels {p} pennies, whats the cents
exam: It is given that {a} holds {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies. Determine the aggregate value of the said coins, expressed in cents.
exam: Ascertain, in cents, the total monetary value of a collection comprising {q.words} quarters, {d.words} dimes, {k.words} nickels and {p.words} pennies.
exam: Whereas a purse contains {p} pennies, {k} nickels, {d} dimes and {q} quarters, state the sum of money therein, in cents.
exam: Compute the value in cents of the coinage in the possession of {a}, namely {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies.
exercise: After Grandad passed away, {a} found {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies in his old coat. How many cents is that?
exercise: Money's a bit tight for {a} this week: all {a.he} has is {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels and {p} pennies. How many cents does {a.he} have?
test: i'm a little short, ok? {q} quarters, {d} dimes, {k} nickels, {p} pennies, that's the lot. how many cents, and don't you dare laugh
